WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.610
We lost!

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.190
What can you do?

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.150
They put us up against third years.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.950
That girl's serve was amazing.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.110
I think she's in the Volleyball Club.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.030
Oh, yeah...

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.330
The older girls said they
were doing softball, right?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:21.950
Did they?

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.000
I checked the tournament schedule earlier,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.500
and it said class 2-1 and class 2-5
will be playing each other.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.630
Class 2-1 and class 2-5...

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.550
Sakurai and Botan
are in class 2-1.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.300
Claire's in class 2-5.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.630
Oh...

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.840
I hear the game starts at 10am.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.510
That's pretty soon.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.970
Wanna go watch?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.020
Yeah!

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.480
They totally ignored me.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.710
The game between class 2-1
and class 2-5 will now begin.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.670
May the best team win!

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.300
Oh, we made it just in time!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.190
Wow!

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.190
Sakura's the pitcher!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.230
She seems like the type who'd
love to be called an "ace."

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.070
Don't you think Botan's
pitches would be faster, though?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.240
But wouldn't that kill the catcher?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.450
Good point.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.870
That wouldn't go well.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.410
Um, the girl playing catcher...

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.870
Will you be all right without a mask?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.540
Yeah. It'd be more work for
the animators if I wore one.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:16.920
Huh?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.720
Let's go!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.640
You can do it!

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.810
Koko! Go for it!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.890
Koko! Keep your eye on the ball!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.810
Claire's class calls her Koko!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.570
I guess it comes from Kokonoe.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.530
Koko, what are you doing?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.490
I know!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.360
She's...

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.990
...signaling that she'll hit a home run!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.700
Go for it, Koko!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.990
Hit it outta the park!

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:46.990
What?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.410
Signaling a home run?

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.700
Crush her, Doumyouji!

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.000
Hit her in the face!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.370
Yeah, kill her!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.380
Class 2-1 is scary!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.460
Play ball!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:03:59.920
Botan...

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.470
Give me a signal for
where I should throw.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.300
But... we never decided on any signals.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.520
That's true. We haven't.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.480
And even if we had, I'm an amateur,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.600
so I don't have the control to
pitch that accurately, anyway.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.940
Then, why?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.530
You give a signal.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.700
I shake my head.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.030
You give another signal.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.950
I nod.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.030
Through this sequence of actions,

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.700
we give the impression that
we know what we're doing,

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.160
and leave class 2-5
shaking in their boots!

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:33.910
I get it.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.920
Then, I'll make some random signals.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.400
Freaky!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.770
What was that?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.730
How'd you do that?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:04:59.440
What?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.770
Can't everyone do this?

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:04.070
Not with just one hand!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.150
Really?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.160
Well, we did what we set out
to do, so what's the issue?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.410
No, we haven't!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.410
The only one shaking
in their boots is me!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.160
More importantly, Sakura...

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.420
What's our strategy for
conquering class 2-5's lineup?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.290
Good question...

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.300
Is Claire actually a good athlete?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.470
I dunno...

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.180
I don't really picture her as one.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.050
Didn't she say she does horse riding?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.770
But how athletic do you
have to be to ride horses?

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.020
I think it's the horse that does
all the work, not the rider.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.060
I've seen her ride
mechanical broncos before,

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.730
but does that have anything
in common with batting?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.030
I dunno...

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.200
I've picked up a horse
and run with it before.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.660
What on earth for?

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.490
I was in my rebellious phase.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.240
I did everything backwards.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.290
Oh, like the "I raced off with
a stolen horse" thing, right?

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.120
Exactly.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.460
Don't just say "exactly"!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.540
I can't believe how
unhelpful that info was!

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.800
Anyway, if we lose this game,

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.930
Claire will lord it over
us for about a week!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.060
Hey, lousy pitcher... I mean,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.770
Sakura, would you pour me some tea?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.480
You're right.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.190
We can't afford to lose.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.070
How about we just pick a fight over
something trivial and start a brawl?

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.820
I get it!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.360
You're a genius!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:31.120
Have you two worked out your plan yet?

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:31.700
Huh?

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.200
Come on, you two...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.330
I've known you two for almost as
long as you've known each other.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.580
The telepathic conversations you have
are loud and clear to me, too.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.840
Oh no!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.550
Our strategy session was leaked!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.100
Just throw the ball already!

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:59.350
Clip-clop, clip-clop, clip-clop...

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.850
Stare...

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:03.480
Let's see...

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:09.030
If you chose C, it means you always speak
your mind when something bothers you,

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.950
and whenever you find an opening,
you can't resist making a retort.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.410
Stare...
Hey, that sounds like me!

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.950
Sounds like you're doing
something fun over there.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.120
Sakura.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.710
Okay, let me give you the next question.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.960
Oh, okay.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.130
You're walking down a hallway at school...

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.090
when you see one of the classrooms on fire.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:30.340
So what do you do?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.220
Um...

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.640
I guess I'd throw water on it.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.680
I'd probably run away.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.270
The correct answer is:

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.060
"Place a handkerchief over your mouth,
get down close to the ground,

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.440
and evacuate in accordance
with the instructions given."

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.320
It wasn't a philosophical question?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.820
During our evacuation drill the other
day, something occurred to me.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.580
We all lack proper
fire safety awareness!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.410
Especially you, Natsuki!

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.660
What happened back there?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.040
Natsuki!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.500
Oh, Sakura.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.630
Why were you so relaxed?

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.920
Weren't you aware that
it was a state of crisis?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.430
If that had been a real
fire, you'd be dead!

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.470
Then you shouldn't have spoken to me.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.010
But part of the problem is the way
the school organizes the drills.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.020
The fire "outbreak" always
happens during class!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.560
And it always starts in either the
science lab or the home ec. room!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.440
It's too convenient!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.610
A fire is not a villain
in a superhero movie!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.190
Um... what does she mean by that?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.530
Villains only cause trouble in cities

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.950
where a superhero happens to live.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.280
There are lots of other places in the
school where a fire could break out!

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:41.660
We have to be on the
lookout at all times!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:42.870
Behind the school, for instance!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.330
Everyone knows that's where
delinquents go to smoke!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.540
It's always been that way!

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.920
Do we have people like
that in our school?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.380
I don't know...

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.720
But I've heard that carelessness with
cigarettes is a major cause of fires.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.260
No, there's actually not much
behind the school that's flammable,

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.350
so even if you do toss them carelessly,
they're not likely to cause a fire.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.230
Huh?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.230
They won't catch fire?

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.890
Then, why did you bring up the subject?

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.400
The real problem comes later...

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.480
When they blog about it and the
comments section catches fire!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.400
That's the kind of "catching fire" you meant?!

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.740
They'd probably hold a school assembly afterward.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.990
How would we evacuate from that?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.620
Just give up and take part in it.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.910
By the way, Botan,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.500
can you tell me what the fire
evacuation acronym, PRD, stands for?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.500
Who, me?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.090
P-Past misdeeds...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.880
R-Revealed for your...

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.300
D-Destruction.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.140
Who are you threatening with that?!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:40.890
Okay, you're dead!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.560
If this was a real fire,
you'd be dead, Botan!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.850
Oh, but I'd be fine.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:46.690
See?

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.860
The flames part in my presence,
so I don't even have to run away.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.440
No nonsensical excuses!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.200
Anyway, Botan,
you just lost a life there!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.030
What, she has continues?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.160
Now, Karin!

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.450
Tell your failing upperclassman the correct answer!

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.830
Um...

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.540
No pushing...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.210
Right!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:08.540
No running...

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.420
Bingo!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:10.580
D...

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:12.960
No dying?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.210
She summed it all up!

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.380
Yes, that's the essence of it.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:23.890
Karin's innocent eyes always see
through to what's really important.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.140
What are you talking about,
you blindly-doting parent?!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.520
You're all hopeless!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.690
The correct answer is: "No pushing,
no running, no discussing"!

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.860
We're bringing you these three!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.280
Why did you do that like
a next episode preview?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:41.870
Incidentally, some schools in some areas
may add "no returning to the scene,"

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.370
"no approaching the site," and
"no leaving evidence behind."

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.410
Are you sure you're not
confusing this with arson?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.210
But there's something I've always wondered...

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.290
The fire evacuation acronym, PRD, stands for:

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.300
"No pushing (buttons), no running
(up your bill), no discussing (gossip)."

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.220
Why can't they just say,
"Don't use your phone"?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.640
Why do they break it up
into individual parts?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.770
You don't get it either?!

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.350
Precious!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.100
Really cute!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.520
Digging prohibited!

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.980
But even if we don't know this stuff,

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.940
there's not going to be
a fire, so we'll be fine.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.820
What? Why not?

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.830
After all, this show's already on episode 3,

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.330
and it hasn't caught fire yet!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:28.950
You said it!

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.660
That was a good one!

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:35.000
You're not supposed to laugh about that!

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.310
If I go through Chichibu from Tokorozawa,

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.520
I can see Lake Yamanaka...

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.520
And from there, Mt. Fuji.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.070
Are you going on vacation?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.820
No, this is my jogging route for tonight.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.410
You've gone way beyond jogging here!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.490
Ah, but I have to get back on the same day.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:11.790
Well, I guess I can make it.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.250
Just how incredibly strong are you?!

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.040
But if I go that far, I should
check out Mt. Fuji, right?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.510
That's not the point...

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.800
But why would you need to run so much?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.090
To be ready in case something happens.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.260
It's important to keep up
your training at all times.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.560
Botan has even started training
in the shower at the pool.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.150
Training in the shower?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.580
You're supposed to outgrow that kind
of "training" in elementary school.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.920
But, Botan, you're
already stronger than a bear.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.710
What do you mean by
"in case something happens"?

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.550
You know.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.420
If we lose popularity as a gag anime,

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.680
we'll have to shift genres
and become a battle series.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.510
That's what she meant by "something happening"?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.470
She's always preparing for a retool?!

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:24.280
Truth is, Hagitsuki-ryuu has an
offshoot called Hagishirabe-ryuu.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.570
You just introduced a scenario out of nowhere.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:29.070
If we lose popularity as a gag anime,

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.540
they'll come after us to take over
as the family's main branch.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.620
What exactly motivates these people's actions?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.830
In hopes of becoming the heir,

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:42.170
The Four Great Kings will come one by one
to try and crush Hagitsuki-ryuu.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.710
There are actually Four Great Kings?!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:48.090
I bet the Four Great Kings arc will
take up about two episodes.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.850
She's planning to beat two per episode!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:52.640
Yeah.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:56.640
But the Four Great Kings aren't the only
pawns Hagishirabe-ryuu has at their disposal.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.770
She's not even denying that she can
defeat the Four Great Kings in two episodes.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.650
There's also the Hagishirabe Five,

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.780
the Hagishirabe Celestial Nine,

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.650
the Hagishirabe Magnificent Ten,

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.280
the Hagishirabe Eleven,

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.160
the Hagishirabe Twelve Heavenly Generals...

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.160
and of course, the Hagishirabe Thirteen.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.700
Wait! These groups keep getting bigger!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.370
Thirteen is just one guy.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.290
He's a silent assassin.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.380
You meant <i>that</i> "13"?!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.790
But it's true...

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.840
It'd be a nuisance to fight that
many opponents one at a time.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.130
We should get them all together...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.800
and have a tournament in
an underground arena.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.470
The Four Bear Kings
didn't stand a chance!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.350
She's not as sweet as her name suggests!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.890
The Bursting Queen:

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.860
Hagitsuki-ryuu, Oohagi Botan!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.770
Kill 'em! Kill 'em!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:44.690
Um...

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.450
Sorry to interrupt such an exciting daydream,

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.450
but why does the arena
have to be underground?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.620
Plus, we don't actually
have an underground arena.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.870
Perhaps I should start
construction on one?

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.870
That's not necessary.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.830
I do have an above-ground arena, but...

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.380
Why do you have one of those?!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.880
Is Hagishirabe-ryuu made up entirely of idiots?

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:13.720
I realize it now!

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.640
She's the real idiot here!

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:22.440
The real problem here is that
Botan is the only fighter among us.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.860
That's not true.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.490
I may be the only one who can
fight the Hagishirabe-ryuu...

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:38.160
But...

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:41.210
No matter how difficult the battle I face,

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.710
as long as you four support me...

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.920
My friends' voices will revive me four times.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.720
Why does each club member
equal one extra life?!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.840
She really does have game brain!

00:15:55.510 --> 00:16:00.270
Natsuki, the looming threat isn't
simply a matter of raw strength.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.350
What?

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:07.900
The Kokonoe family's riches make it
extremely powerful in politics and business.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:12.320
But there are other families
that hold similar influence.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.200
If we lose popularity as a gag anime,

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.290
they will all start moving to
upset the existing hierarchy.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.580
She brought up another scenario!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.830
Then, we will enter into a social battle of wits.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:25.670
What?

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.790
But the writers don't know
anything about that stuff!

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.920
We'll do, like...

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:32.840
stock—

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.680
stock tra—

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.220
insider trading...

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.430
of stock.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.930
Their lack of knowledge is already showing!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:47.900
A tournament in an underground
arena or a social battle of wits...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.230
Natsuki.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.530
You're mistaken if you think a retool will
shift this series to the battle genre.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.030
Huh?

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.200
When popularity drops,

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.240
they add more pointless fanservice!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.660
We're going in that direction, too?!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.660
Every time you open a door,
someone's getting changed!

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.380
When the wind blows, the pantyshots abound!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.590
Why?!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.800
Bras fall from the second floor!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.800
Does that even count as fanservice?!

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.100
That's the world that awaits us!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.470
What kind of world is that?

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.850
Should I have a shower
installed in the club room?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.940
I don't think that's necessary.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:27.810
No, wait.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.480
If we have a shower in the club room,

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.360
I can train any time I want, can't I?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.940
I told you, outgrow that in elementary school!

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:38.910
Besides, that's only if we need a retool...

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.700
And why was it only me in
all those fanservice shots?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.160
But we are being retooled.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:50.000
This is the third episode of our show,
and we still haven't caught fire!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.880
Huh? You were being serious?!

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.260
When it comes to late-night anime,

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.010
episode 3 is where people decide
if they'll keep watching or not.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:04.470
Our entire future's riding on how
well episode 3 draws in the crowd!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.270
That scene earlier where
Botan was training...

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:11.190
A lot of the shots were from weird angles...

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.940
Is that what you're talking about?!

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:13.940
Exactly.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:19.490
Having an episode about sports is another
sign that the retooling has begun.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.580
Wait, wait!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.950
This isn't even right!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:31.130
Whew, I'm glad I made my signal there.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:31.960
No, no...

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.960
That signal isn't covering anything!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.710
Look! Your whole body is blurred out!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.340
And look what happened to this scene!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.430
Sakura-sa— No.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:46.430
Ignorant peasant!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.520
I'll let you be my personal servant,

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.270
so make me some tea on your hands and knees!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.190
Claire's character
has completely changed!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.940
Mine has, too!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:03.370
That means we have to do everything we
can to make them laugh, no matter the cost.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.500
Okay, since you haven't said anything
since the commercial break, Karin...

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.160
Y-Yes?

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.920
Say something funny!

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.750
That will be the punchline for this segment.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.840
It also has to sum up
everything we've talked about.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.220
She's asking the impossible!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.760
Um, let's see...

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:27.970
What do Chronicles of the
Going Home Club punchlines

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.810
and the ball in a one-player
softball game have in common?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.690
You're going with a riddle?

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.270
What do they have in common?

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.570
They keep getting thrown away!

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:38.780
Good one!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.320
Karin...

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.160
you've grown over the course
of three episodes, too.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.120
I have nothing left to teach you.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.700
Um... Was it really that good?

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.210
Oh, yeah!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.330
Ah, can I say one more thing?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.250
What'll it be this time? An acrostic?

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.710
No...

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.510
Oh, I know!

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.380
"These softball jokes are
reaching fever <i>pitch</i>,"

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.340
or something like that, right?

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.600
No, it's something I've been wanting
to point out for some time...

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.180
This isn't episode 3.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.850
It's episode 4.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:13.730
What?

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.320
B-B-But what do we do about the retool?!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.950
We'll have to pound each
other in a tournament!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.990
We don't have time to
round up fighters now!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.620
Then, I'll just have to get naked!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.620
Don't be so hasty!

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.750
Let me go, Natsuki!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:30.790
That's it!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.410
I have to do it before it's too late!

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.080
The ending song!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.540
Haven't we used that joke enough already?!

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.250
No. That's not what I mean.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.340
It's the smallest retooling we can do.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.630
Change the ending song!

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:46.340
What? We can do that now?

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:47.930
Hello, it's me.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:51.560
Could I request a new ending song?

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.690
Yes. Right now!

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.950
The... The Kokonoe Corporation is formidable...

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:35.450
You sang that, didn't you, Botan?

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:38.580
I can't turn down a request from Claire...

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:41.710
So who were you duetting with?

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:44.090
Yo!

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.260
Claire here.

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:50.840
Honeypot ants store large amounts
of nectar in their bodies.

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:53.930
But as a result, they're sometimes
eaten by humans as candy.

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:55.220
It's kinda sad, isn't it?

00:22:58.020 --> 00:22:59.100
And two more!
